  /* ==========================================================================
     BRITAIN, FRANCE AND GERMANY - 93 VEHICLES THAT HAD NO MODEL OF THEIR OWN
     ==========================================================================
     MEASURED before this block: the game held 117 British, French and German
     ground vehicles and NOT ONE of them had a model. This table had 258 rows
     covering nato, pact, pla, roc and kpa and not a single gbr, fra or deu
     row, so modelKeyFor() fell through to the first same-role peer and a
     Challenger 2 drew as an M1A2 SEP v3, a Leopard 2 as an M1A2, and a
     Warrior, a Marder, a Puma and a VBCI all as an M2A3 Bradley.

     Note what a row costs a vehicle as well as what it buys. render3d.js
     getModel() sets the ERA_KIT repaint only when key !== def.id, so a
     vehicle with its own row stops getting the generic era paint and bolt-on
     kit. That is the same bargain every one of the 258 existing rows already
     makes - the row IS the period, through `camo` and `extras` - and a
     correct Leopard 2 silhouette in flat NATO three-tone beats an Abrams in
     period paint.

     WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE: sam, tel and radarv. js/sam3d.js and
     js/tel3d.js hand-author those launchers and BOTH load after this file, so
     a row here would REPLACE a detailed Rapier or Pluton with rocketPack's
     generic tube honeycomb - a straight regression. Britain's ground-based
     air defence was towed for its entire Cold War, which is a national fact
     and not a missing row.

     Every value below was validated mechanically against js/armour3d.js
     before it landed: every hull, turret, mantlet, susp, skirts, camo and
     kind against the sets the builder actually tests, and every extras key
     against its addExtras branches. kind "tank"/"wheeled"/"open" and extras
     "netting"/"snorkel"/"sideMg" are inert house convention - the existing
     table uses them 95, 41, 14, 68, 49 and 16 times - and are kept for
     consistency rather than trimmed. */


